window.VD=window.VD||{};window.VD["vw/touran-1t3"]={"touran-1t3-activate-bluetooth-on-rns-315":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate Bluetooth on the RNS 315.  </p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION: Not all RNS-315 are equipped with a Bluetooth module.</strong> </p>\n<figure><table><thead><tr><td>Module compatibility list</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>3C0 035 279</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 A</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 B</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 C</td><td>Yes (conditional)</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 D</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 E</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 F</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 G</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 H</td><td>Yes</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 J</td><td>No</td></tr><tr><td>3C0 035 279 K</td><td>No</td></tr></tbody></table></figure>\n<p>You can also remove the RNS 315 from its slot to check. Behind it, you’ll find a label with the RNS-315’s MAC address.<br/>If the MAC address contains only zeros (MAC: 00:00:00:00:00:00), your RNS-315 is not equipped with the Bluetooth module. </p>\n<figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns_315_j_mac_non-6328b9e5.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns315_mac_oui-eed1a386.webp\"/></figure>\n</figure>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>3</strong><br/>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Uncheck the “Telephone Transceiver inactive” box</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/RNS315_3C0-035-279_Module37_Byte3-74e93c9c.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns-315-bt-8b82eb41.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-activate-daytime-running-lights-drl-only-with-headlight-switch-in-auto-position":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate daytime running lights (DRL) only when the light <strong>switch</strong> is in Auto position.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>26</strong>: <br/>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Daytime Running Light (DRL) only active with Assistance Driving Light (ADL) active”.  </p>","touran-1t3-activate-driving-school-mode-rcd-210-rcd-310":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to add a Driving School mode view to the RCD 210, RCD 310 that displays turn signals, speed … (Also ideal for accompanied driving) <br/><br/><br/><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“56 – Radio</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose<strong>“Channel 2</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>7</strong> – On this same page, there is a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>On this menu, select<strong>“1</strong>” and confirm.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/golf6_golf_vi_fahrschulfunktion-5b883ac1.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-activate-headlamp-washers":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the headlamp washers.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>20</strong>: Bit<strong> 5</strong>: Check “Headlight Washer Installed”.</p>","touran-1t3-activate-hidden-menu-rns-315":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate the hidden menu in RNS 315.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Developer mode (temporary)</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong><em>Enabled</em></strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart RNS 315.</em></p>\n<p><em>To launch the Hidden Menu, press SETUP (for 6s)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3C0-035-279_Module37_Adaptation_Developer_mode_tem-59109da4.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns-315-bt-8b82eb41.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-activate-hidden-menu-rns-510":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Activates the hidden menu in RNS 510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program.<strong><strong>56 – Radio</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose <em><strong>Channel 50</strong> </em>then set the value to <strong>1</strong></p>\n<p><em>Restart the RNS 510.</em></p>\n<p><em>To launch the Hidden Menu, press SETUP (for 6s)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/1T0-035-680-C_Module37_Adaptation_Channel50-1a7d6a90.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510-1024x821-d0438887.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-activate-mood-lighting":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate ambient lighting.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 Ambient lighting activation. 1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>20</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Footwell Lights installed”.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 Ambient lighting setting :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Channel <strong>27</strong> “Footwell Lighting Dimming (with open Door)”.</p>\n<p><em>Set a value between 0 and 200 (for 100% lighting, set 200).</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 3 Activate ambient lighting while driving :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>12</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Check “Footwell Lights withbTerminal 58d active”.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 4 Ambient lighting control while driving :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> Channel<strong> 35</strong> “Footwell Lighting Dimming (with Terminal 58d)”.</p>\n<p><em>Set a value between 0 and 200 (for 100% lighting, set 200).</em></p>","touran-1t3-activate-rearview-camera-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the rearview camera after it has been installed on the RCD 510/330/360/440 and RNS 315/510 (retrofit).  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>37 – Navigation</strong> ” (RNS) or “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>” (RCD)<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5 – </strong> Select byte <strong>3</strong><br/>. Then set bit <strong>6</strong> to “Rear View Camera (RVC) installed/active.”</p>\n<p><strong><strong><strong>Line 2 (Optional, if parking assist is available)</strong> <strong>:</strong></strong></strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>10 – Parking Assistance</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>5 – </strong> Select byte <strong>0</strong><br/>. Then set bit <strong>5</strong> to “Rear View Camera installed.”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/CA86A611-2F74-4201-B791-7A74BC107A01-1024x482-c9f00e16.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>Hardware upgrade :</strong></p>\n<p>The camera’s video cable is connected to the infotainment control unit. It is installed in the glovebox.   <br/><br/>The two pins from the backup camera are used in the 12-pin Quadlock connector (blue).<br/><br/>Quadblock Assignment :<br/><br/>Pin 6 = video line<br/>Pin 12 = shielding</p>","touran-1t3-activate-rns-510-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> To enable installation of the RNS 510 to replace the original RCD-310 (retrofit).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 (RNS-510 Activation in the Gateway):</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19-Gateway CAN</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Installation List</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – <em>Check “37- Navigation</em></p>\n<p><em>Click on “Save coding</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 (Media-in activation</strong>)<strong>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte <strong>0</strong></p>\n<p><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “AUX-Input Connection Monitoring active”.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 3 (RNS-510 without Dynaudio</strong>)<strong>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 1</strong></p>\n<p><em>Bit <strong>0-7 </strong>: Select “00 Sound System not installed”.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 4 (Original speakers</strong>)<strong>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 2</strong></p>\n<p><em>Bit <strong>0-7</strong>: Select “04 4 Speaker Channels (Front and Rear)”.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 5 (RNS-510 theme</strong>)<strong>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Encoding 07</strong>.” Then click ” <strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>.” </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 7</strong></p>\n<p><em>Bits <strong>4-5</strong>: Select one of the 3 themes</em><br/><em>“00 Display Variant: Highline”</em><br/><em>“10 Display Variant: Sportsline”</em><br/><em>“20 Display Variant: Premium”</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2B758E5F-ACB4-418C-BBBB-B61B0F3A298B-186113f1.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 6 (Display of navigation information on the ODB</strong>)<strong>:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 7</strong></p>\n<p><em>Bit <strong>7</strong>: Check “Communication Instrument Cluster via Operation and Display Protocol (BAP)”.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 6 (Vehicle selection displayed when OPS is activated) :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 9</strong></p>\n<p><em>Bit <strong>0-7</strong>: Select “05 Optical Park System &amp; Interior Graphics: VW Golf (5K1)”.</em></p>\n<p>Exit the module and save your changes. The RNS-510 must now be restarted for the changes to take effect. Press both arrows and the star for 6s.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510-1024x821-d0438887.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-activate-rns-510-voice-control":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate voice control on the RNS 510 (SDS).  </p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION:</strong> RNS 510 firmware must be version v2660.</p>\n<p>Activating voice control brings up the “Voice control” menu in the RNS 510’s SETUP menu.</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on “<strong>Select</strong>”. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <strong><strong>“37 – Navigation</strong></strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>3</strong>, check the box for<strong>“Bit 1: Microphone Diagnostics active</strong>”.</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>7</strong>, uncheck the box for<strong>“Bit 1: Voice Control inactive</strong>”.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/RNS510_Menu_Commande_Vocale-bf5955d7.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>To install the microphone, connect the microphone lead to the rear of the RNS 510. Connect to pins (Mic-)C1 and (Mic+)C7. </p>","touran-1t3-activating-coming-leaving-home":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to activate Coming Home and Leaving Home. And add it to the ODB (MFA)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>12</strong>:<br/>Disable bit <strong>2</strong><em>“Coming-Home Mode (0 = Automatic / 1 = Manual)</em>”<br/>Set bit <strong>2</strong> for display in ODB (MFA)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/cominghomeg6-f70c52d7.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Byte <strong>17</strong>:</p>\n<p>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Check “Coming-Home (CH) active”<br/>Bit <strong>6</strong>: Check “Leaving-Home (CH) active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/cominghomeg62-efef7c12.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/cominghomeg63-3c107aa3.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/cominghomeg64-189ea28a.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/cominghomeg65-b5621af6.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-adapting-brake-assist":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to configure brake assist.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“03 – ABS</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select Channel <strong>09</strong> (Brake Assist from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p><em>Choose a value</em><br/> 0<em>“medium” </em><br/>1 “low” (with low assistance, the brake pedal will be harder and more pressure will be required to brake)<br/>2 “high” (with high assistance, the brake pedal will be softer and less pressure will be required to brake)</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/assistfreing6-05b83882.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-add-daytime-running-lights-drl-to-odb":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to add daytime running light (DRL) settings to the ODB (on-board computer).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>15</strong>: Bit <strong>7</strong>: Check “Daytime Running Light (DRL) Active Adaptation (MFA+)”</p>","touran-1t3-adjusting-the-volume-of-the-reversing-beep":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to adjust the volume of the reversing beep.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“10-Station assistance</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong>Select Channel: <em>“rear warning buzzer volume”. </em> </p>\n<p>Adjust value accordingly<br/>(default: 5)</p>","touran-1t3-automatic-closing-of-windows-and-roof-in-case-of-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Automatically closes the windows and sunroof when it rains. </p>\n<p>The vehicle must be locked using the remote control for this to work. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vitregolf561-c90da3e5.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “2” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vitregolf56-9439cbb9.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears, select byte<strong> 0</strong> and check bit <strong>2</strong>, <strong>“Rain Closing active</strong>,” to enable the windows and roof to close when it rains:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Vag-Com-Fermeture-Automatique-des-vitres-5-d61c5dd9.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>7 – After completing this step, click on the “Exit” menu</p>\n<p> Then click “OK”</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Vag-Com-Fermeture-Automatique-des-vitres-7-353fb01b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2: </strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Select <em>Byte<strong> 4</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>5</strong>: Check “Comfort Operation Windows/Sunroof via Rain Sensor (0 = nonrecurring / 1 = permanent)” </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>6: </strong> Check “Comfort Operation Windows/Sunroof via Rain Sensor (Rain Closing) active” </em> </p>","touran-1t3-automatic-door-locking":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to set automatic door locking from 15km/h.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Channel 04 (Auto-Lock drop-down list) <em>Set value to <strong>1</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 If the adaptation channel is not enabled.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Power Plant.</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2 : </strong> Check “Auto-Lock active”. </em> </p>","touran-1t3-automatic-door-unlocking":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to set automatic door unlocking when the key is removed.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> Channel 05 (drop-down list (Auto-Unlock)) <em>Set value to <strong>1</strong></em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 If the adaptation channel is not enabled.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Power Plant.</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0 : </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Auto-Unlock active”. </em> </p>","touran-1t3-automatic-headlamp-activation-from-140-km-h":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to automatically switch on the lights when the vehicle is travelling at over 140 km/h. </p>\n<p>(The lights will automatically go out if the vehicle is travelling at less than 60 km/h) </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>0</strong>, Bit <strong>0</strong>: Check “Highway Light Function active above (140kph/90mph)”. </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-automatic-headlamp-activation-in-case-of-rain":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to automatically turn on the lights when it’s raining and the wipers have been triggered.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “2 EPIRBs” module from the drop-down list and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>0</strong> Bit <strong>1: </strong> Check “Rain Light Function Active”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Calc09-RLS-140kmhBit0-Octet0-4f74e4e9.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-automatically-folding-mirrors":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Automatically folds mirrors when vehicle is locked.  </p>\n<p>For 4th generation door modules (models from 2013) activation is possible with Vag-Com VCDS  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>42 – Driver’s door</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Security Access – 16</strong>” then enter the code<strong>“04354</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Select Channel:<strong>“System_Parameter_0-System</strong> Parameter Byte8” from the drop-down list.<br/><br/>Replace Value <strong>90</strong> (if several values, 90 is in the middle).</p>\n<p>Set value according to mirror opening mode: <br/> – <strong>95</strong> (mirrors<em> will deploy when door is opened)</em><br/><em> – <strong>99</strong> (mirrors will deploy when ignition is switched on)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/DCA8744A-30AB-4C05-B633-4F3B76D90C50-4f152256.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>For 3rd generation door modules (models up to 2011) activation is only possible with VCP.</p>\n<p>Click on Guided Functions then select the “Convenience” module on the right then “Activation automatic folder mirrors in UDS door control units (Passat/ Tiguan / Jetta)”.</p>\n<p>Setting, Command: “Folding with driver door” or “Folding with ignition” = with driver door or with key</p>\n<p>Engine/Car type : CAN TP20 1K0/5K0</p>\n<p>Start the procedure, but don’t forget to save the Conductor 42 door module with access code 04354.</p>","touran-1t3-brake-assist":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to configure brake assist.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“03 – ABS</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select Channel <strong>09</strong> (Brake Assist from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p><em>Choose a value</em><br/> 0<em>“medium” </em><br/>1 “low” (with low assistance, the brake pedal will be harder and more pressure will be required to brake)<br/>2 “high” (with high assistance, the brake pedal will be softer and less pressure will be required to brake)</p>","touran-1t3-change-the-rcd-rns-510-theme":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to change the display theme of the RCD 510 and RNS 510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>” for RNS510 and “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>” for RCD510.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 7</strong></p>\n<p><em>Bit <strong>4-5</strong>: Select from 3 themes</em><br/><em>“00 Display Variant: Highline</em><br/><em>“10 Display Variant: Sportsline</em><br/><em>“20 Display Variant: Premium</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2B758E5F-ACB4-418C-BBBB-B61B0F3A298B-186113f1.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/69C76009-6EC7-465A-A676-8E39BA840A6B-6689b9e0.webp\"/><figcaption>Highline</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3A58F148-9FBB-4DD8-BF05-E03A5351E3A8-e9b6cb9b.webp\"/><figcaption>Sportsline</figcaption></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4894A3B7-2ED2-4A75-9D46-CA3BFCF5A76C-8fb8de15.webp\"/><figcaption>Premium</figcaption></figure>\n<p>Exit the module and save your changes. The RCD / RNS 510 must now be restarted for the changes to take effect. Press both arrows and the star for 6s.  </p>","touran-1t3-changing-the-image-of-the-rcd-rns-ops":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to change the vehicle image of the OPS (parking aid) on the RCD 510/330/360/440 and RNS 315/510.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Turn on the ignition, then launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>37 – Navigation</strong> ” (RNS) or “<strong>56 – Radio</strong>” (RCD)</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Encoding 07</strong>,” then ” <strong>Long Coding Helper</strong> “</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Choose Byte<strong> 6</strong> or <strong>9</strong></p>\n<p><em><em>Select</em>the vehicle <em>from the drop-down menu</em>:</em><br/><br/>00 = via CAN<br/>01 = Polo 6R<br/>02 = New Beetle<br/>03 = New Beetle Cabrio<br/>04 = Scirocco<br/>05 = Golf 5<br/>06 = Jetta<br/>07 = Golf 6 Variant<br/>08 = Golf 6 Cabrio<br/>09 = Touran<br/>0A = Golf Plus<br/>0C = Tiguan<br/>0D = Sharan<br/>0E = EOS<br/>0F = Passat 3C<br/>10 = Passat Limousine<br/>11 = Passat Variant<br/>13 = Caddy<br/>14 = T5<br/>2C = Skoda Octavia<br/>2D = Skoda Octavia Kombi<br/>2E = Skoda Superb Kombi</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/IMG_0864-978ed9ed.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>Exit the module and save the changes. You must now restart the RCD or RNS for the changes to take effect.  Press and hold the two arrows and the star for 6 seconds.</p>","touran-1t3-closing-windows-after-door-opening":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Closes windows and sunroof after removing key and opening door.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>” then click on “<strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> Choose <em>Byte<strong> 4</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Uncheck “Power Windows/Sunroof </em>disabled after door opening<em>” </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>7: </strong> Check “Power Windows/Sunroof enabled after Terminal 15/Ignition OFF </em>”  </p>","touran-1t3-comfort-blinker":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to set the number of flashes for the “Comfort flashing” option.  <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5 </strong>– Select<strong>“Comfort Turn Signal”</strong> from the drop-down list </p>\n<p>Choose a value between 1 and 5 for the number of flashes</p>","touran-1t3-coming-leaving-home-with-fog-lamps":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Enables fog lamps to be used for Coming Home and Leaving Home.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte<strong> 17</strong>: <br/>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Coming-Home (CH) via Fog-Light active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5_774-e325de60.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-coming-leaving-home-with-xenons-halogen":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Activates xenon (or halogen) headlamps instead of fog lamps for Coming Home and Leaving Home.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>17 </strong>:  </p>\n<p>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Uncheck “Coming-Home (CH) via Fog-Light active”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5_774-e325de60.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-coming-home-settings":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to configure the Coming-Home behavior.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>The Coming-Home timer starts when the door opens<br/><em>Byte <strong>12 </strong>:  </em><br/><em>Bit<strong> 0 </strong>: Check “Coming-Home Timer (0 = Start with Term.15 OFF / 1 = Start with Door Opening)”.   </em></p>\n<p>The Coming-Home timer starts when the ignition is turned off<br/><em>Byte <strong>12</strong>:  </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: Uncheck “Coming-Home Timer (0 = Start with Term.15 OFF / 1 = Start with Door Opening)”   </em></p>\n<p>Coming-Home is activated manually with a headlight flash<br/> Byte<em> <strong>12</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit<strong> 2</strong>: Uncheck “Coming-Home Mode (0 = automatic / 1 = manual)” </em>.  </p>\n<p>Coming-Home switches on automatically<br/> Byte<em><strong> 12 </strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “Coming-Home Mode (0 = automatic / 1 = manual)” </em>.  </p>","touran-1t3-corner-lights-activation":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to activate cornering lights with fog lamps.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong> then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”. Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/4-Activation-des-feux-en-virage-sur-Golf-5-et-6-f4e51c90.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>6</strong> – In the window that appears, select  </p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>12</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Check “Cornering Light Activation Time limited”.</em></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>14 </strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>7: </strong> Check “Cornering Lights via Front Fog Lights active”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5-Activation-de-la-fonction-Cornering-Lights-via-F-255e876b.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>7</strong> – After this operation, click on the “Output” menu<br/>Then validate “OK”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6-Activation-de-la-fonction-Cornering-Lights-via-F-2a08cc40.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-corner-lights-in-reverse":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to activate the cornering lights with the fog lamps when reversing.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>26</strong>: Bit <strong>6</strong>: Check “Enabling Cornering Light with Reverse Gear active”.</p>","touran-1t3-correction-of-odb-consumption-display":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: to correct the fuel consumption display on the on-board computer.  </p>\n<p><strong>Modification only possible on Mid/High range models</strong>. <br/><em>Note: modifications affect the display of instantaneous consumption, average consumption and fuel quantity.</em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on “<strong>Select</strong>”, then click on <strong>“17 – Instruments”</strong>. <strong>Procedure:</strong> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation- 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 03</strong> <em>“Consumption Correction”.</em></p>\n<p><em>Adjust consumption correction factor between 85% and 115%.</em> <em>(base value: 100)</em></p>\n<p><em>Example 1: Calculation based on volume per distance (e.g. l/100 km): DIS: 9.3 l/100 km. Actual: 9.8 l/100 km. (100, 9,8 / 9,73 ? 105,38) Channel 3 will be changed from 100 to 105 <br/>Example 2: Calculation based on volume distance (e.g. MPG is: DIS: 23 MPG. Actual: 24 MPG. (100, 23/24 and 95.83) Channel 3 will be changed from 100 to 96</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/correction-consommation-odb-d51db18e.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-cruise-control-activation-retrofit":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to activate GRA cruise control (retrofit). </p>\n<p><strong>Modification only possible after retrofitting cruise control switch and <a href=\"https://wiki.ross-tech.com/wiki/index.php/Steering_Wheel_Control_Module_Versions\" rel=\"noopener\" target=\"_blank\">check that your multifunction steering wheel is compatible (midline or highline)</a>.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>01 – Motor</strong> “.<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on ” <strong>Coding II (11) or Login 11</strong> “. </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/regulateur1-1c279499.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Then enter code <strong>11463</strong>, then <strong>OK</strong> (Do It!)</p>\n<p>The code 11463 is used to <strong>activate</strong> the controller, to <strong>deactivate</strong> it if necessary the code is 16167.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/regulateur2-6871f13e.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>16 – Multifunction handwheel</strong> “.<br/><br/>4<strong>– </strong>Click on ” <strong>Coding – 07</strong> “. </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/regulateur3-945b80f3.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Options: We note in the penultimate section (0xxxx<strong>?</strong>x):<br/><br/>0 = No regulator installed (CCS not installed)<br/>1 = Regulator installed with 6 positions on a separate switch (CCS with 6 positions …. etc)<br/>3 = Regulator installed with 4 positions on the blinker switch (CCS with 4 positions via Blinker Stalk)</p>\n<p>So replace the “<strong>?</strong>” with the 3 for commodo regulator.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 3:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”, then click on ” Select</strong> “. <strong><strong>01 – Engine</strong></strong> ” .<br/><br/>4 – Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>” then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select byte<strong>“5</strong>“<br/>Check bit<strong>“5</strong>” Cruise Control System (CCS) installed</p>\n<p>Or byte <strong>6</strong> bit <strong>0</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/regulateur5-1024x491-af7739d1.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-daytime-running-lights-off-drl-with-handbrake-on":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>deactivates the daytime running lights when the handbrake is engaged.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>11</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0</strong>: This is a hidden bit; you must replace the last <strong>0</strong> on the right side of the binary number with <strong>a 1</strong>. (<strong>10001000</strong> =&gt; <strong>10001001</strong>)</em></p>","touran-1t3-deactivate-automatic-rear-wiper":"<p> <strong> Purpose:</strong> to deactivate automatic activation of the rear wiper.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on <strong>“Long Coding Helper”</strong>:</p>\n<p><em>Byte<strong> 21</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Uncheck “Automatic Rear Window Wiping with Front Wiper at ‘Interval’ active”.</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Uncheck “Automatic Rear Window Wiping with Front Wiper at ‘Permanent’ active”.</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>6</strong>: Uncheck “Automatic Rear Window Wiping with Reverse Gear active”.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/5K0-937-086-M_Module09_Byte21-499f6b9b.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-deactivate-brake-pad-warning-light":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to disable the brake pad wear warning light on the OBD (On-Board Diagnostics) system, for example, for brake pads without a sensor or if the sensor is malfunctioning / Brake Pad Warning Light Deactivation. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>17 – Instruments</strong>“.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Cliquer sur « <strong>Codage – 07</strong> » puis cliquer sur « <strong>Assistant Codage Long</strong>« .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>: “<br/>” Then uncheck bit <strong>0: </strong> <strong>“Brakepad warning active/installed”</strong> </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant-frein-d4619ec9.gif\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-deactivate-esp":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate ESP completely.  </p>\n<p><strong>ATTENTION: Only valid for vehicles from 2012.</strong> </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“ABS Brake 03</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Change the value of byte 6, replace <strong>00</strong> by <strong>80</strong><br/>Change the value of byte 14, replace <strong>00</strong> by <strong>01 (do not change byte 14 for TDIs)</strong> </p>\n<p>Simply press the ESP button to deactivate traction control (ASR)</p>\n<p>Press and hold the ESP button for 4s to deactivate the ESC as well.</p>","touran-1t3-deactivate-windshield-washer-indicator":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to deactivate the windshield washer indicator on the ODB (on-board computer).  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/>Then uncheck Bit <strong>2: </strong>“<strong>Washer Fluid warning active/installed</strong>”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/laveglace-edc83d4f.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-delete-belt-alarm":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> To suppress the audible alarm and the warning light on the speedometer when driving without a seatbelt.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>:<br/>Then uncheck Bit <strong>1: </strong>“<strong>Seatbelt warning active/installed</strong>”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6J0-920-802-J_Module17_Byte1-5e3ec890.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/voyant_ceinture_de_securite-296648a9.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-disable-bluetooth-connection-beep":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: Disables the beep when a device successfully connects to the car radio’s Bluetooth.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“77 – Telephone</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select “Bluetooth acknowledgement signal” from the value list</p>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– Select <strong>“Off” </strong>from the second drop-down list</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/7P6-035-730-C_Module77_Adaptation_Bluetooth_acknow-580a5d47.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-disable-plate-light-control-odb-led-error":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Disables license plate light control. Useful when installing LED bulbs without resistance or for error prevention.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p>Byte <strong>23</strong>:  </p>\n<p>Bit <strong>6</strong>: Uncheck: “Lamp Monitoring (Cold) License Plate Lamps Active”.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/led_plaque5-odt_147-d36567c5.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-door-lock-unlock-confirmation-beep":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>Enables vehicle lock/unlock confirmation with beeps (with alarm)  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then connect the other end to your vehicle’s diagnostic port.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong> Select Byte <strong>5</strong>:</p>\n<p>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Locking Confirmation via Horn Enabled”</p>\n<p>Bit <strong>4: </strong> Check “Unlocking Confirmation via Horn active” </p>","touran-1t3-electronic-differential-lock-xds":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the electronic differential lock (XDS).  </p>\n<p>The electronic differential lock (XDS) is an extension of the well-known EDS function. However, XDS does not react to acceleration slip, but rather relieves pressure on the inside front wheel when cornering. XDS applies pressure to the inside wheel during cornering from the hydraulic ESP to prevent slippage.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>03 – ABS</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<p><em>Byte 17 : </em><br/><em>Bit 3: Tick “(Extended) Electronic Differential Lock (XDS – PR-UG3/UG4) active/installed”</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 XDS setting.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>03 – ABS</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10 </strong>”.</p>\n<p>Channel 36 (Electronic Differential Lock (XDS) in drop-down list)</p>\n<p><em>Choose a value</em><br/> 0<em>“medium” </em><br/>1 “low” <br/>2 “high  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/xdsg6-567d8998.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-flash-mode-lights-during-emergency-braking":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: activates the brake/turn signal lights in flash mode during emergency braking.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket. <br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select the “0” module and click on “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>16</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>1</strong>: Check “Emergency Brake Flashing via Brake Light active” (to activate brake lights)</em><br/><em>Bit <strong>2</strong>: Check “Emergency Brake Flashing via Turn Signal active” (to activate turn signals)</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/emergencybreakg6-7e26fa37.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-full-sunroof-opening-with-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows the sunroof to open fully when using the “Comfort Open” function with the remote control. </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – With the engine off and the ignition switched off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostic port.<br/><br/><strong></strong> 2 – Turn on the ignition and launch the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click<strong>“09 – Central Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click <strong>“Encoding 07,”</strong>then click “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte<strong> 3</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit 0: Check “Comfort Opening for Sliding Sunroof active” </em><br/><em>Bit 1: Check “Comfort Closing for Sliding Sunroof active” </em><br/><em>Bit 2: Uncheck “Comfort Opening Type for Sunroof (0 = open/ 1 = lift)” </em><br/><em>Bit 5: Check “Comfort Operation via Remote Control active” </em> </p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “Select”.<strong>4F – Power Plant II </strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click <strong>“Encoding 07,”</strong>then click “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em>Byte<strong> 1</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>0: </strong> Uncheck “Comfort function Sliding Roof: Tilted”</em></p>","touran-1t3-hill-hold-control":"<p><strong>Purpose: Enables </strong>Hill Hold Control (Hill Start Assist).  </p>\n<p>Hill Hold Control maintains brake pressure for a few seconds after the brake pedal is held down for an extended period.</p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes</strong>” (or “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes” </strong>).<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>“</p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>16: </strong></em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Check “Hill Hold Control (HHC/PR-UG1/UG4) active/installed”</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2: Hill Hold Control Settings.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes</strong>” (or “<strong>03 – ABS Brakes” </strong>).<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p>Select <strong>Channel 58</strong> (Hill Hold Control (HHC) from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p>Select a value:<br/>0 “normal”<br/>1 “earlier” (restarts with lower acceleration)<br/>2 “later” (restarts with higher acceleration)</p>","touran-1t3-lock-cd-dvd-eject-button-on-rns-510":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: locks/unlocks the RNS 510’s CD/DVD eject button.  </p>\n<p><em>Protection against theft of your navigation DVD.  </em></p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/> 3 – Click on ” <strong>Select”</strong>, then click on ” <strong>Select</strong> ” and run the VCDS program. <strong><strong>37 – Navigation</strong></strong>” .</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <em><strong>Channel 43</strong> (Ejection Lock)</em> then set the value to <strong>1</strong> <em>(CD/DVD Ejection Lock active)</em></p>\n<p><em>Restart the RNS 510.</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510-1024x821-d0438887.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-lower-passenger-mirror-when-reversing":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> automatically lowers the passenger mirror when reversing.  </p>\n<p>The mirror adjustment knob must be in position<strong>“R”</strong> for the passenger mirror to lower automatically.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>09 – Centrale Elec</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>” .</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/retrogolf61-d4a12d4d.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/retrogolf62-a22a3a65.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – In the window that appears, select byte<strong> 4</strong> and check bit <strong>3 “</strong> <strong>Mirror Lowering With Reverse Rear </strong>” to activate mirror lowering when shifting into reverse gear:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/retrogolf63-d65eea5e.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>6 </strong>– After this operation, click on the “Output” menu, then validate “OK”.  </p>\n<p>A message appears to inform you that the coding has been accepted.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 2:  </strong></p>\n<p><strong>3 –</strong> Click on<strong> “Select” </strong>, then click on<strong> “52 – Passenger door”.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><em>Add <strong>256</strong> to the value</em></p>","touran-1t3-memory-for-heated-seats":"<p><strong>How it works :</strong> When you switch on the heated seat(s), as soon as you remove the key from the ignition the setting is immediately switched off. With this activation, when you switch the ignition back on, the seat will have returned to the level at which you left it.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“08 – Climatronic</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – On this page, at the very top, there is a drop-down menu.<br/>In this drop-down menu, choose  </p>\n<p>“<strong>Retention of driver’s seat heater level</strong>” for <strong>Driver’s seat heater memory</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3AA-907-044-AG_Module08_Adaptation_retention_of_dr-51646659.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>and/or<strong>“Retention of passenger’s seat heater level</strong>” for <strong>Passenger seat heater memory</strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/3AA-907-044-AG_Module08_Adaptation_retention_of_pa-61b11e06.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><br/><strong>6</strong> – On the same page, there’s a second drop-down menu at the bottom<br/>of the page.<br/>Select<strong>“active</strong>” and confirm.</p>","touran-1t3-modify-power-steering-hardness":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to adjust the hardness of the power steering for a softer or harder steering wheel.  </p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“44 – Direction assistée” / “44-steering assist.</strong><br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Adaptation – 10</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select<strong> Channel 1 </strong>, <em>set a value between<strong> 1</strong> and <strong>15</strong> depending on your hardness preference</em>.</p>\n<p><strong>Or Line 2: (If channel 1 is unavailable)</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“44 – Direction assistée” / “44-steering assist.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4 </strong>– Click on<strong>“Coding – 07</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select :</p>\n<ul>\n<li>xxx1x for smooth steering</li>\n<li>xxx2x for sports management</li>\n<li>xxx3x for hard steering</li>\n<li>xxx4x for harder steering</li>\n<li>xxx5x for very hard steering</li>\n</ul>","touran-1t3-mute-push-to-talk-button":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong> Allows you to reconfigure the Push-To-Talk (PTT) button at the bottom left of your multifunction steering wheel to function as a mute button for the audio volume. (2010 and later)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/></p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>16 – Multifunction Steering Wheel.”</strong><br/></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding- 07</strong>”. then click on<strong>“Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5 – </strong>Select <em>Byte<strong> 1</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>3</strong>: Uncheck </em><em>“Multi-Function-Steering-Wheel (MFSW) with Push-To-Talk (PPT) Button installed</em>”.</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/pttg6-da3300eb.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>The Push-to-Talk (PPT) button now acts as a mute button.</p>","touran-1t3-needle-check":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> activates needle sweep when the car is started. (Needle Sweep)   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>10-Adaptation</strong>” then in the window that appears, click on the drop-down menu to choose a channel and select the “<strong>Staging</strong>” channel, if unavailable select the “<strong>indicator_celebration</strong>” channel:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg6-9456b738.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – In the “<strong>New value</strong>” box, click on the drop-down menu and select “<strong>active</strong>”. Once this new value has been entered, click on “<strong>Save</strong>”:</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/checkg62-c8918051.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-oil-temperature-on-the-odb":"<p><strong>Purpose: </strong>to activate the Oil Temperature Display in your Grand ODB.  </p>\n<p>Some cars don’t have this sensor available in the ODB, including some Golf MK6s and Sciroccos, whether TDI or TSI, and even R versions. Here’s a short tutorial to help you activate it and make it available in your ODB.  </p>\n<p><em>ATTENTION: Modification cannot be activated on all counters.</em> </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on “<strong>Select”</strong>, then click on “<strong>17 – Instruments</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “<strong>10-Adaptation</strong>”, then in the window that appears, click on the drop-down menu and select this byte: <strong><em>(7) WIV : Service interval coding Oil level and temperature transmitter</em></strong></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Vag-Com_01_Sonde_Temperature-d-huile-Golf6R-TSI-TD-913f0cb0.webp\"/></figure>\n<p>English version: Coding For Service Interval Extension TOG</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/Vag-Com_01_Sonde_Temperature-d-huile-Golf6R-TSI-TD-6650dcd4.webp\"/></figure>\n<p><strong>5 –</strong> <em>Select ”  <strong>Oil level/temp. transmitter connected to instrument holder   </strong>“in the second drop-down list</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/1Z0-920-843-G_Module17_Adaptation_7-WIV_v2-73e7e7f3.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/vw_temp_huile_odb-b53aaa02.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-ops-speed-camera-display-on-car-radio-screen":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Enables the display of OPS speed cameras on the car radio screen.  </p>\n<p><strong><em>Please note: The vehicle must be equipped with a compatible car radio (RCD-310, RCD-510, RNS-315, RNS-510).</em></strong> </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>10-Parking Assistance</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong></strong> 4 – Click on “<strong>Security Access – 16</strong>,” then enter the code “<strong>71679</strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Click on “<strong>Coding – 07</strong>,” then click on “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong>Select <em>Byte<strong> 0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit <strong>4</strong>: Tick “Optical illustration active”.</em></p>","touran-1t3-programming-a-remote-control":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to program the remote controls that will be used with the vehicle for central locking and unlocking.  </p>\n<p>⚠️ <strong>WARNING:</strong> This procedure does not allow you to program remote controls with the vehicle’s immobilizer.<br/>If your vehicle is equipped with a <strong>KESSY</strong> remote control <strong>(05 – Access/Ignition Authorization)</strong>, you cannot program a new remote control using this procedure.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong><strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 01 ( </strong>“Remote Control Adaptation” from the drop-down list)</p>\n<p>Enter the number of keys to program, then click <strong>Save</strong>.<br/>Next, press the <strong>Unlock</strong> button on each remote control to be programmed for at least 1 second. The flashing lights will confirm the process.<br/>All keys must be programmed in a single session, one after the other.<br/>Programming all keys must not take longer than <strong>15 seconds</strong>.<br/>You can add up to <strong>7 remote controls</strong>. If the <strong>[Test]</strong> and/or <strong>[Save]</strong> buttons are grayed out and unclickable, the module likely has all 7 slots filled; delete the remote controls using the <strong>“Reset Remote Controls”</strong> tutorial.  </p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/programmertelecommande-51bf4068.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-top-up-quantity-displayed-on-odb":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Displays the amount of fuel needed to completely fill your tank on the OBD (On-Board Computer). <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“17 – Instruments</strong>“.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Adaptation – 10” </strong>.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>“Volume to be Replenished” </strong>from the value list.</p>\n<p>Select ” <strong>Yes</strong> ” in the second value list.</p>","touran-1t3-resetting-the-remote-controls":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Resets the settings for all remote controls associated with the vehicle. </p>\n<p><strong>⚠️ WARNING:</strong> After completing this procedure, all remote controls will be deleted and will need to be reprogrammed using the <strong>“Program a Remote Control”</strong> tutorial <strong>.</strong><br/>If your vehicle is equipped with a <strong>KESSY</strong> remote control <strong>(05 – Access/Start Authorization)</strong>, you cannot delete the remote controls using this procedure.</p>\n<p><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click <strong>“Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong><strong><strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></strong></strong>.”<br/><br/><strong>4 </strong>– Click on “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>”.  </p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select <strong>Channel 00</strong></p>\n<p><em>Set the value to <strong>0</strong> and save</em></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/6Q0-959-433-E_Module46_Adaptation_Channel00-caced031.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-selective-door-unlocking":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Allows you to configure selective door unlocking.  </p>\n<p>When unlocking the vehicle, only the driver’s door is unlocked. To unlock all doors, press the remote control’s unlock button twice.   </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure: </strong><br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Channel 03 (drop-down list: Selective (Single) Door Locking) <em>Set the value to 1</em></p>\n<p><strong>Line 2 If the adaptation channel is not enabled.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “<strong>Select</strong>,” then click “<strong>09 – Power Plant.</strong>“</p>\n<p><strong>4 – </strong> Click “<strong>Encoding – 07</strong>,” then “<strong>Long Coding Helper”</strong></p>\n<p><em>Byte <strong>0</strong>: </em><br/><em>Bit<strong> 3: </strong> Check “Selective Central Locking active (Single Door Locking)” </em> </p>","touran-1t3-sound-reduction-on-ops-activation":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> Automatically lowers speaker volume when OPS is activated.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure </strong>: <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1 :</strong></p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>”, then click on<strong>“10-Station assistance</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click “<strong>Adaptation – 10</strong>.”</p>\n<p><strong>6 – </strong>Select <em>Channel<strong> 08</strong> (Audio Volume Lowering): </em><br/><em>Set value to<strong> 0</strong></em></p>","touran-1t3-speed-limit-display-rns-510":"<p><strong>Purpose </strong>: to display the speed limit on the RNS 510 navigation screen.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/> 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/> 2 – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1</strong>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select</strong>” then click on<strong>“37 – Navigation</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on<strong>“Coding 07</strong>”. Then “<strong>Long Coding Helper</strong>”.</p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select Byte<strong> 7</strong><br/>Activate Bit <strong>2</strong>: Speed Threshold for Destination Input active</p>\n<p>+ use voice command to activate Bit 3: Speed Threshold for Speech Destination Input active</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/2B758E5F-ACB4-418C-BBBB-B61B0F3A298B-186113f1.webp\"/></figure>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/rns510speed-9dcbaa67.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-start-stop-deactivation":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to disable Start and Stop completely.  <br/><br/><br/><strong><em>Only compatible with Gateway 7N0! Temperature deactivation method. </em></strong> <br/><br/><br/><strong>Proceed :</strong> <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/><strong>3</strong> – Click on<strong>“Select”</strong>, then click on<strong>“19 – CAN Gateway</strong>”.<br/><br/><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Long Adaptation – 0A”</strong>.<br/><br/><strong>5</strong> – Select Channel<strong>“13</strong><br/><br/><strong>6</strong> – In new value, select<strong>“D02000</strong>” (default value = <strong>002000</strong>) then validate.<br/></p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/gof6startstop-1024x528-699ec970.webp\"/></figure>","touran-1t3-tear-wiping":"<p><strong>Purpose:</strong> to activate the windshield wipers once more after using the windshield washer, in order to remove any remaining water from the windshield.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure:</strong> <br/>1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/>2 – Switch on the ignition, then run the VCDS program.<br/><br/><strong>Line 1:</strong><br/><br/>3 – Click on ” <strong>Select</strong> “, then click on ” <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.</strong>” . Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program. 1 – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.</p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on <strong>“Coding – 07”</strong> then <strong>“Long Coding Helper”.</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select byte <strong>1</strong>, <br/>Check Bit <strong>3</strong></p>","touran-1t3-activate-daytime-running-lights-with-fog-lamps-drl":"<p><strong>Purpose</strong>: Allows fog lights to be used as daytime running lights.  </p>\n<p><strong>Procedure</strong>: <br/><strong>1</strong> – Engine off, ignition off, connect your official VAG-COM VCDS cable to the computer, then plug the other end into your vehicle’s diagnostics socket.<br/><br/><strong>2</strong> – Switch on the ignition and run the VCDS program.</p>\n<p><strong>Line 1</strong><em> </em>:</p>\n<p><strong>3</strong> – Click “ <strong>Select</strong>,” then click “ <strong>09 – Cent. Elect.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>4</strong> – Click on “ <strong>Code 07.”</strong></p>\n<p><strong>5</strong> – Select module “0” and click “Long Coding Helper”:</p>\n<p><strong>6 –</strong> <em>Byte <strong>14: </strong> </em><br/>Check <em>Bit <strong>1</strong> ” </em><em>Daytime Running Lights (DRL) via Fogs Active</em>“</p>\n<figure><img decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" src=\"img/drlantibrouillardg6-df7e4302.webp\"/></figure>"};
